e suite, while matrix row 4 reports the property as driven. That is the same shape this Story has been rejected for repeatedly — a row that claims a property its test reaches only at the trivial value — so close it properly:\n4|1. Commit one multi-record row that resolves EVERY event's raw reference against its own line, with the offsets asserted (not merely the bytes). Add a labelled harness row for the offset-accumulation bug that the new row kills, and cite it from matrix row 4 and TRACEABILITY. No production change.\n5|2. P3-u/v/w/z: state the optional-boolean null bound; add rows (or the message-only statement) for the body type and required gates; name the empty-directive edge; note `body:null` on unknown types.\n6|3. P3-x/y/aa: `doc.go` \"nine\" becomes \"ten\"; the optional message tidy-ups; drop the self-entry from `MANIFEST.sha256`.\n7|4. Re-run the battery twice on the final tree, re-run tracecheck, and report the ratio you MEASURE.\n8|Procedure — READ THIS, TRUNK HAS MOVED. The sibling Story STORY-260830-ptxkqe landed while you were in review: origin/main is now 42d5a95 (PR #55), and it touches `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json`, README.md and LOGBOOK.md — the same files this leaf owns. Run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-32ypr2` FIRST. Then audit every path in `git diff --name-only c3aae73 42d5a95` that also appears in your `git status`, and in particular: the ownership registry must be MERGED, never replaced — trunk now carries the ptxkqe Story's rows and yours must be added alongside them, after which `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` must be RE-DERIVED from the merged registry (the digest in your candidate is stale the moment the merge happens); README and LOGBOOK edits stay additive on the NEW content and must never restore the old bytes; the README measured-coverage subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on the merged tree and still pass the landed `readme_coverage_pin_test.go`. Keep the candidate UNCOMMITTED. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Run your own package tests and the harnesses BEFORE handoff, then the full configured suite once (read the command count from the candidate config). Update the results with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-32ypr2 --role developer` so revision 4 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in.\n9|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt died mid-way, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n10|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 4.","final_result":true}}}
