{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5bd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b4ea-fb92-7cf3-9cd5-04cb5a5f5467"},"sequence":313,"recorded_at":1780531400000621,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"16aac74a-8f80-4da1-94ce-cabce45ae87b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"16aac74a-8f80-4da1-94ce-cabce45ae87b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"16aac74a-8f80-4da1-94ce-cabce45ae87b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b4eb-a8d3-7d00-b257-9e22c52a7c4f"},"task_id":"01a0b4eb-a8d3-7d00-b257-9e22c52a7c4f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b4eb-a8d3-7d00-b257-9e22c52a7c4f","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-32ypr2/TASK-260830-32ypr2_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-32ypr2 Results (rev4) — test-unknown-encrypted-and-incomplete-events\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree\n4|(`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q`); no commit on the Story branch.\n5|Branch tip: `5cc9449` (the replayed `TASK-260830-2g5be6` checkpoint over\n6|trunk `42d5a95`); `origin/main` is `42d5a95` at handoff — the refresh\n7|below ran FIRST, before any other work, because the branch tip\n8|`3005d78` (over `c3aae73`) no longer descended from the authority.\n9|\n10|## Refresh (ran first)\n11|\n12|Sibling STORY-260830-ptxkqe landed as PR #55 (`42d5a95`) while rev3\n13|was in review, so `task-board worktree refresh-candidate\n14|TASK-260830-32ypr2` ran before anything else: `refresh_advanced`\n15|onto `42d5a95` with checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay for both\n16|checkpoints (`517c457` LOGBOOK sha256\n17|`7394f679…30a630`, `3005d78` LOGBOOK sha256\n18|`3712a8d6…213935`; trunk blocks kept newest-first, incoming blocks\n19|appended below, both preserved). The audit then restored trunk bytes\n20|for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/axpane`,\n21|`internal/termbind`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/fencing`,\n22|`internal/terminalbackend` — the refresh had carried their\n23|pre-refresh absence/bytes as deletions and reverts) and MERGED the\n24|co-owned files onto the new trunk bytes instead of replacing them:\n25|LOGBOOK (leaf entry newest-first on top of trunk), README (all six\n26|package sections kept; figures re-derived), the ownership registry\n27|(152 cases / 74 rows; every trunk row intact, verified by hash),\n28|and the four pin tests. `task-board.config.json` is byte-identical\n29|to the new HEAD (verified with `cmp`; 30 commands). `git status`\n30|shows only candidate paths (LOGBOOK, README, 2 clonesnap prose\n31|files, 7 traceability files, untracked `internal/cloneproject/`).\n32|\n33|## Inherited work vs this run\n34|\n35|Inherited the rev3 candidate tree verbatim (uncommitted working tree:\n36|the complete `internal/cloneproject` package, registry rows,\n37|README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits) plus the rev3 review packet\n38|(verdict RUN-260918-d009f2, evidence tar, probe logs, reviewer\n39|plants). No partial rev4 edits existed. This run verified the rev3\n40|claims firsthand where re-touched (the class-closure grep below),\n41|then applied every rev3 finding. Nothing is accepted from prior\n42|runs: every exit quoted here was observed on the final tree in this\n43|run.\n44|\n45|Class-closure kept (verdict Section 0, re-verified, not re-done):\n46|`grep -n 'NewDecoder\\|Unmarshal' internal/cloneproject/*.go`\n47|(non-test) shows only `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at\n48|`strictMembers`, the five exact-name `json.Unmarshal` reads, `Body\n49|= members[\"body\"]`, the `CheckUint53Bounds` version read,\n50|strict-map body reads, and the sealed-manifest map read — no second\n51|decoder. No production file changed this run (test-plus-matrix\n52|only); the rev3 alias-axis tests, narrowings, and prose stand\n53|untouched.\n54|\n55|## Finding-by-finding table (rev3 verdict → change → test → evidence)\n56|\n57|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n58||---|---|---|---|\n59|| P2-e raw-addressability measured only at offset 0 (all seven `mustResolveRef` sites on single-record members; `RV-offset-drops-newline`, `RV-offset-line-number`, `RV-evidence-offset-second-line` SURVIVED 2/2 while matrix row 4 claimed the property driven) | `TestNormalizeMultiRecordRefsResolveAtAssertedOffsets`: three-record member (multibyte `message/user`, unknown `frobnicate`, foreign `reasoning/encrypted`); EVERY event's `RawRefs[0]` resolves to its own line with offsets asserted (`0`, `len(l1)+1`, `len(l1)+len(l2)+2`) and lengths asserted; matrix row 4 + TRACEABILITY cite it | The new test | `mutants/run1/N-offset-newline.log` + `run2` (labelled behaviour swap, killer); `crosscheck-RV-offset-line-number.log` and `crosscheck-RV-evidence-offset-second-line.log` (reviewer shapes KILLED firsthand, exit 1, files restored byte-identical); `pkg-cloneproject-v.log` |\n60|| P3-u optional-boolean null bound unstated (`\"live_followup\":null`, `\"live_attestation\":null` admitted as false) | STATED as a bound (doc.go, TRACEABILITY, matrix §A row 46 + §C + §D) and pinned by `TestNormalizeNullOptionalBoolsDecodeAsFalse` (null attestation stays uncallable history; null followup completes; live surface empty) | The new test | `pkg-cloneproject-v.log` |\n61|| P3-v body-level type and required-member gates carry no negative row (`RV-member-text-number`, `RV-body-required-skip-text` SURVIVED 2/2) | Rows shipped (stronger than the message-only statement): `body_text_number` (`{\"text\":123}` refuses `is not a string`), `body_live_attestation_string` (refuses `is not a boolean`), `body_missing_text` (`{}` refuses `misses member \"text\"` — the message pins the required gate, since under the plant it refuses with the type message instead) | The new rows | `mutants/run1/N-body-text-number.log`, `N-body-bool-string.log`, `N-body-required-skip-text.log` (+ `run2`; 3 narrowings, each admitt