{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cbab","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b4ea-fb92-7cf3-9cd5-04cb5a5f5467"},"sequence":1072,"recorded_at":1780531400002139,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"16aac74a-8f80-4da1-94ce-cabce45ae87b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"16aac74a-8f80-4da1-94ce-cabce45ae87b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"16aac74a-8f80-4da1-94ce-cabce45ae87b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b4ee-5921-7682-8cb8-2001fa5d8284"},"task_id":"01a0b4ee-5921-7682-8cb8-2001fa5d8284","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b4ee-5921-7682-8cb8-2001fa5d8284","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Clone Bundle Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-24z2b3)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/clonebundle`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|The Story's FINAL leaf carries the `internal/traceability` registry\n7|bindings and re-pin; this file is the first-leaf clause record.\n8|\n9|## Why this package validates instead of canonicaljson\n10|\n11|The `canonicaljson` closed-shape registry keeps\n12|`rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows for\n13|`clone-raw-object-manifest`, `clone-capture-manifest`,\n14|`canonical-session`, and `canonical-event` 1.0.0, and that table's\n15|census pins every row. Replacing them would fork shape ownership, so\n16|this package is the validating owner: it reuses\n17|`canonicaljson.Canonicalize` (byte transform),\n18|`canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons\n19|(Blob Descriptors; never the attesting entry, per the provhost\n20|no-attestation bound),\n21|`sessadapter.DecodeTuple` (Environment Tuples),\n22|the `environ` scalar gate set (`CheckStringBounds`,\n23|`CheckUint53Bounds`, `CheckDigest`, `CheckUUIDv7`,\n24|`CheckTimestamp`, `CheckSortedUniqueStrings`,\n25|`CheckSortedUniqueDigests`, `CheckExtensions`, `StringLength`,\n26|`DecodeStrictObject`) through one-line delegating wrappers in the\n27|`sessadapter` convention, keeping only package-specific rules\n28|(sanitizer, exclusion, coupling, reconciliation, extension values),\n29|`scalar` (digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, paths),\n30|`hosttrust` (row-21 exclusion matchers), and\n31|`localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob` (blob install). No rule is\n32|reimplemented where a landed owner exists.\n33|\n34|## Clause map\n35|\n36|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n37||---|---|---|\n38|| 13.14.1 Raw Manifest closed envelope + self ID | `BuildRawObjectManifest`, `DecodeRawObjectManifest` | `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestRawManifestRefusals/decode` |\n39|| 13.14.1 RawObjectEntry class subset (no credential/auth/runtime/lock) | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals/build` (5 class rows) |\n40|| 13.14.1 sorted unique entries, total_bytes sum | `buildRawEntries`, `decodeRawEntries` | `TestRawManifestRefusals` (unsorted, duplicate at build + decode, total mismatch, not-an-array, 65536 maximum, byte_count overflow) |\n41|| 13.14.1 sanitized native key, never an AX Session ID | `SanitizeNativeKey` | `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer`, raw/capture/session/event refusal rows |\n42|| Sanitizer exact bound (pinned text leaves scope open) | `SanitizeNativeKey` | `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer` corpus: refuses empty, Cc+C1 controls, Cf/Zl/Zp invisible format marks (U+200B/U+2028/U+2029), invalid UTF-8, absolute paths, UUIDv7, password-colon-before-@ (schemed or schemeless), case-folded `urn:ax:`; admits spaces, bare `@`, bare `:` |\n43|| Row 21 exclusion allowlist at construction | `refuseExcludedMember` | `TestRawManifestExcludesTrustMaterial`, `TestCaptureManifestExcludesTrustMaterial` |\n44|| 13.14.1 CaptureItem 9-class vocabulary | `ValidCaptureClass`, `buildCaptureItem`, `decodeCaptureItem` | `TestCaptureClassVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestCaptureItemRefusals` |\n45|| 13.14.1 included/excluded content rule | `checkItemDisposition` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (6 content rows) |\n46|| 13.14.1 always-excluded classes never included | `alwaysExcludedClass` | `TestCaptureItemRefusals` (4 class rows) |\n47|| 13.14.1 exact excluded_classes | `excludedRowClasses`, `excludedClassesExact` | `TestExcludedClassesExactGate`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/decode` |\n48|| 13.14.1 core-derived raw_complete + reconciliation | `deriveRawComplete`, `VerifyCaptureReconciliation` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n49|| 13.14.1 unknown blocks maximal_safe | `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` |\n50|| 13.14.1 Capture Source Basis union | `DecodeSourceBasis`, `buildSourceBasis` | `TestSourceBasisRefusals` |\n51|| 13.14.1 Capture Boundary union, stable proof coupling | `DecodeCaptureBoundary`, `buildBoundary`, `checkProofCoupling` | `TestBoundaryRefusals` (incl. input_blocked row), `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n52|| 13.14.1 unstable is core-created, G2 rejects | `buildBoundary` (Core), `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestBoundaryRefusals/build_core-only_unstable`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnstableArchive` |\n53|| 13.14.1 NativeIdentity closed shape | `DecodeNativeIdentity`, `EncodeNativeIdentity` | `TestNativeIdentityRoundTrip`, `TestIdentityRefusals/native_identity`, `TestEncodeNativeIdentityRefusals` (encode validates extensions, native keys, kind text) |\n54|| 13.14.1 source_identity_digest terminal digest | `IdentityDigest` | `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip` |\n55|| 13.14.1 WorkspaceBinding closed shape, normalized cwd | `DecodeWorkspaceBinding`, `checkCwdRelative` | `TestIdentityRefusals/workspace_binding` |\n56|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session + Actor rules | `BuildCanonicalSession`, `DecodeCanonicalSession` | `TestBuildCanonicalSessionRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals` (incl. decode external-null-parent, version, not-an-array, 1024-actor maximum) |\n57|| 13.14.1 Canonical Event envelope + 26 kinds + visibility | `BuildCanonicalEvent`, `DecodeCanonicalEvent`, `ValidEventKind` | `TestEventKindVocabularyIsPinned`, `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals` (incl. ordinal/offset/length overflow, version, not-an-array, raw_refs/reason-codes maxima), `TestCanonicalEventPayloadValueModel` |\n58|| 13.14.1 SourceEvidence + RawReference + synthesized coupling | `DecodeSourceEvidence`, `buildSourceEvidence`, `checkEvidenceCoupling` | `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/evidence` |\n59|| 13.14.1 message-like content blocks, 64 KiB inline bound | `checkPayload`, `checkContentBlocks` | `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` (block rows incl. null content/descriptor, top-level duplicate, 64 KiB boundary) |\n60|| 13.14.1 contiguous ordinals from zero | `CheckOrdinalContiguity` | `TestOrdinalContiguity` |\n61|| 13.14.1 immutable generations | `ParseGeneration`, `Generation.Equal`, `CheckDigestsEqual` | `TestGenerationRefusals`, `TestBoundaryRefusals` |\n62|| 13.14.1 reverse-DNS extensions, no normative reference | `encodeExtensions`, `checkExtensionsClosed` | contract round trips + `bad extensions` rows in every refusal table |\n63|| 1.6 AX number model + nested duplicate refusal on extension values, every site | `checkExtensionsClosed`, `checkExtensionValues`, `checkAXNumberLiteral` | `TestRawManifestRefusals/extension_values` (1.5, 2^53, -(2^53), 2^60, exponent, nested float/unsafe, nested duplicate incl. resealed) + `TestExtensionValueModelAtEverySite` (one value-fault row per admission site, 17 rows) |\n64|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `stringLength` via `environ` | `TestMultibyteStringMeasure` (300-char/600-byte admit, 512 admit, 513 refuse) |\n65|| 1.6 text MUST be valid UTF-8 at Build (no rewrite-and-continue to U+FFFD) | `validText` at every Build string admission, `EncodeNativeIdentity` identity sanitize, `encodeExtensions` text walk | `TestBuildTextMustBeValidUTF8` (22 rows + collision pair, sealed-bytes U+FFFD assertions) |\n66|| 13.14.1 one item per plan candidate at construction | `checkPlanItemMatch` | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/build_plan_match` (extra, missing, renamed candidate, duplicate plan keys) |\n67|| 13.14.1 content block inline-XOR-descriptor | `checkContentBlocks` | `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` (neither, both) |\n68|| 13.14.1 duplicate raw keys refused | `VerifyCaptureReconciliation`, `deriveRawComplete` | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/reconciliation` (duplicate raw/plan keys, derive direct) |\n69|| 13.14.1 source_identity_digest over sanitized bytes | `IdentityDigest` (sanitizes before encoding, re-decodes before hashing) | `TestIdentityDigestIsStable`, `TestIdentityDigestRefusals` (bad kind, bad extension key, unsanitized opaque/session) |\n70|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor identity + byte-count agreement | `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` (with entry identity link) | `TestBlobAgreementRefusals`, `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestVerifyRawManifestDescriptorsRefusals` |\n71|| 10.2 entry names the verified descriptor | `buildRawEntries`, `VerifyRawManifestDescriptors` | build `descriptor id mismatch` row, `TestVerifyRawManifestDescriptorsRefusals` (fetch/absent/wrong/link) |\n72|| 10.2 no-replace install (fsync + verify + atomic) | `InstallRawBlob` via `localstore.PutBlob` | `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent`, `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` (forged claim, short/long bytes) |\n73|| 7.8 tuple/probe/manifest/discover/inspect reuse | `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` at every `source_environment` | `bad tuple` rows in raw/capture/session/event tables |\n74|| Byte-identical construction | all Build entries | `RoundTrip` tests rebuild and compare bytes |\n75|\n76|## Durability bound\n77|\n78|This package performs no durable write: `InstallRawBlob` delegates\n79|every byte to `localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob` (no-replace install,\n80|fsync, size/digest verification, quarantine on collision). The\n81|landed crash/idempotency evidence for that discipline lives with\n82|`internal/localstore` (`object_store_test.go`,\n83|`object_store_fault_unix_test.go`, projection fault suites);\n84|`TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` proves the delegation end to end\n85|(double install agrees, tampered bytes refuse). No second write\n86|path exists in this package.\n87|\n88|## Stated bounds (sibling scope)\n89|\n90|- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries past the envelope\n91|  (which facts a kind may carry) are the normalization sibling's\n92|  registry. The Section 1.6 value model on every payload member\n93|  (integer literals, |n| <= 2^53-1, no fraction/exponent,\n94|  duplicate-free nested objects, depth bound) is enforced here for\n95|  every kind by `checkPayloadValues`, and payload numbers decode to\n96|  exact int64, so sealed bytes never round or collapse:\n97|  `TestCanonicalEventPayloadValueModel` (build + decode negatives\n98|  per non-message kind, sealed-bytes exactness, resealed decode,\n99|  message regression, depth bound).\n100|- `-0` admits in extension values and payloads (sealed as `0`, the\n101|  JCS form); leading-`+` (`+1`) and leading-zero (`01`) literals\n102|  are refused at the frame gate (`decodeStrictObject` reports \"not\n103|  a JSON object\", since the tokenizer cannot read them). The model\n104|  refuses fractions, exponents, and magnitudes at or beyond 2^53.\n105|- `BoundaryInput.Core` is caller-asserted; the real unstable-archive\n106|  protection is `RefuseUnstableForTarget` at target admission.\n107|- `InstallRawBlob`'s and `VerifyDescriptorAgreement`'s descriptor\n108|  member-parse arms (`blob_id`/`size`/self-field/object shape)\n109|  repeat the owner grammar after `CalculateObjectIdentity` already\n110|  enforced it (`validateBlobDescriptor` requires a digest\n111|  `blob_id`, a uint53 `size`, and the `descriptor_id` self field):\n112|  defense in depth, unreachable on failure, pinned by the owner\n113|  suite; the agreement/install negatives pin the claim comparison\n114|  and the store size/digest enforcement end to end.\n115|- The raw-manifest `total_bytes` uint53 overflow arm needs entry\n116|  byte counts summing past 2^53-1 with agreeing descriptors (real\n117|  payloads cannot reach it): defense in depth behind the\n118|  per-entry uint53 arm, which carries a `byte_count overflow` row.\n119|- C1 beyond U+0085 (e.g. U+009F), the fraction arm of\n120|  `checkAXNumberLiteral` (subsumed by `ParseInt`), and the exact\n121|  256/257 depth edge are owner-informational: the class is pinned\n122|  (U+0085, `1.5` refusals, the 300-deep payload refusal) without\n123|  pinning every member.\n124|- The extension text walk trusts the marshaled form of values with\n125|  a computed representation (custom `json.Marshaler`\n126|  implementations): it validates strings, map keys, and elements\n127|  reachable by shape, not bytes a `MarshalJSON` method computes.\n128|  Every realistic extension value (JSON-shaped maps, slices, and\n129|  strings, plus struct values) is walked, pinned by the\n130|  `raw_extensions*` rows of `TestBuildTextMustBeValidUTF8`.\n131|- Per-kind Canonical Event payload fact registries beyond the\n132|  Section 13.14.1 envelope enforced in `checkPayload` (normalization\n133|  sibling).\n134|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n135|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n136|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n137|- Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize operation wiring\n138|  (stays owned by `sessadapter`); this package owns the contracts\n139|  those operations produce, not the operation frames.\n140|- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\n141|  (Story FINAL leaf).","final_result":true}}}
