{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e42b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b4ea-fb92-7cf3-9cd5-04cb5a5f5467"},"sequence":4208,"recorded_at":1780531400008411,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"16aac74a-8f80-4da1-94ce-cabce45ae87b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"16aac74a-8f80-4da1-94ce-cabce45ae87b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"16aac74a-8f80-4da1-94ce-cabce45ae87b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b516-234e-77b0-8df9-547f6ae51bb9"},"task_id":"01a0b516-234e-77b0-8df9-547f6ae51bb9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b516-234e-77b0-8df9-547f6ae51bb9","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-118-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cd /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree && git rev-parse origin/main && sed -n '1,40p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Check trunk position and logbook head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"42d5a959aa523572d2745d44f828d41a0b2d72b3\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/cloneproject` implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity closure — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session + Canonical Events from a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed Clone Raw Object Manifest, and blob bytes fetched through the real store layout. Unknown native types and unknown-class members become raw-addressable `opaque_event` records (`unknown_native_event`, ranges resolve to exact bytes); foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning` (`foreign_encrypted_payload`/`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, no content members); foreign instructions pin `low` authority and never reach the effective snapshot; tool calls resolve `completed` only with their result, else `aborted` history (`unsafe_pending_action`) with an always-empty live surface (pending needs a live work order, which capture never carries); source usage counts source-only; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (25 tests incl. the 33-row refusal table plus unstable/drift entries, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure; 88.9% statement coverage); 49 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite and one verified cross-kill (the encrypted-gate plant also reddens the protected-message test). No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `69d156d9…2235052a` via the gate, shown in results); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, `clone-projection-fidelity`, `session-adapter-call-binding`; `tracecheck` green at cases=144, full=4, partial=8, sliver=5, unevidenced=47, clauses 63/569 with `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` admitted; `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (scanner sees no RFC 2119 line — closed-shape sentences only — so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\\n- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n- REV2 (rework of review RUN-260918-320878, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): P1-a CLOSED — envelope+body frame decodes delegate to `environ.DecodeStrictObject` at `strictMembers` (lone-surrogate/duplicate/trailing faults refuse with the fault named; the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate); 4 new refusal rows + 4 narrowings. P2-c CLOSED — `bodyUint53` and the envelope version delegate to `environ.CheckUint53Bounds` (string-typed numbers refuse; per-member failures merge into one \\\"is not a uint53\\\" refusal while the ledger sum keeps \\\"exceeds uint53\\\"); string rows + 5 narrowings. New P3 rows: actor-order determinism (3 actors x12, `N-actors-sort`), both type/protection agreement arms, trailing bytes, protected-tool fold-skip, result-status vocabulary, size arm with its own message + drift row, unknown+protected body refusal; P3-i non-JSONL bound stated + pinned, P3-l null-directives pinned, P3-c per-edge rows stated as bounds (the \\\"representative\\\" claim removed); P3-j unions the 10.2 binding to 11 cases (10.2#2 gains `localstore-immutable-blob-install`); P3-k relabels (`N-empty-projection` single-member class, `N-overflow-truncate` behaviour swap). P2-a: one decision line per inherited advisory group (1,2,3,5,6,7b deferred with owners; 4/P3-e closed as a stated bound; 7a/P3-ζ closed by P1-a; 7c/P3-ζ′ rewritten as a deferred-unification bound) and the two false-prose sites rewritten. P2-b: 7.8#1 rebound to the new `session-adapter-frame-bound` case (`DecodeRequestFrame` + the oversize/edge tests, sessadapter owner); cases 144→145; digest re-derived `4bd01143…` gate-computed; README prose fixed (7.8 bound to sessadapter, Nine cases, admissions list, 10.2 union note).\\n- REV2 EVIDENCE: 62 narrowing + 2 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; the six re-anchorable reviewer plants (R1,R2,R5,R6,R7,R8 shapes) KILLED firsthand by the new tests. AC: 38 of 38 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev2).\\n- REV3 CORRECTION (rework of review RUN-260918-a4ffef, CHANGES REQUESTED; no base move, still `3005d78` over trunk `c3aae73`): the REV2 sentence \\\"the later struct read is exact because the rewriting/guessing shapes never pass the gate\\\" was FALSE — the struct decode matched member names case-insensitively and took the last match, so a case-folded alias overrode the claimed value while the strict map admitted it as a distinct extra. The second decoder is DELETED: `parseNativeLine` now reads the six claimed envelope members from the strict map by exact name (`json.Unmarshal(members[name], ...)` + `Body = members[\\\"body\\\"]`), and no lenient re-read of the envelope remains anywhere after the strict gate (verified by grep: the only struct decode is gone; every other `Unmarshal` reads a strict-map member or a sealed manifest map by exact key).\\n- REV3 (same run): P1-b CLOSED — `TestNormalizeCaseAliasEnvelopeIgnoresUnclaimedMembers` pins all six alias axes through `Normalize` (kind in both document orders, origin/authority, protection/promotion refusal, body/content, evidence identity, actor/attribution refusal) plus an unrelated-extra control; six `N-alias-*` narrowings each restore the case-folded read for exactly one member and all KILLED. P2-d CLOSED — positive `reasoning_summary` row (`TestNormalizeReasoningSummaryProjectsInternal`) + routing-swap narrowing. P3-m capture status asserted for every emitted kind (`TestNormalizeCaptureStatusExactForEveryKind` + partial-stamp narrowing); P3-n last-wins pinned by two native instructions (`TestNormalizeLastNativeInstructionWins` + fold-first narrowing); P3-o external kind pinned (`TestNormalizeExternalActorSealsAsExternal` + kind narrowing, and the reviewer-exact R7 swap KILLED firsthand); P3-p unknown-type-without-body refusal row + required-member narrowing (reviewer R1 shape); P3-q `text:null` stated as a bound (seals empty inline content, pinned) with `ciphertext:null` noted harmless; P3-r `N-pending-aborted` relabelled add-arm and the shared-site `N-strict-*` rows disclosed as one gate/two call sites (harness + TRACEABILITY + matrix + results); P3-s per-edge bound text now names `native_type` (reviewer R2 re-run firsthand: SURVIVED, inside the bound). Five prose sites corrected (`native.go` comments, TRACEABILITY rows, README exact-name sentence, this entry, results).\\n- REV3 EVIDENCE: 72 narrowing + 3 labelled rows KILLED + control SURVIVED, battery green twice with per-plant raw logs; reviewer R1/R4/R5/R6 shapes adopted as shipped narrowings, R7 adopted as a condition narrowing with the exact swap also KILLED firsthand, R3 still KILLED (untouched line). AC: 45 of 45 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev3).\\n- REV4 (rework of review RUN-260918-d009f2, CHANGES REQUESTED with no P1; the rev2 rework is CLOSED AT THE CLASS per the verdict's Section 0 — kept untouched): P2-e CLOSED — `TestNormalizeMultiRecordRefsResolveAtAssertedOffsets` resolves EVERY event's `RawRefs[0]` against its own line with offsets asserted (`0`, `len(l1)+1`, `len(l1)+len(l2)+2`, multibyte first line), plus labelled behaviour-swap `N-offset-newline`; the reviewer's `RV-offset-line-number` and `RV-evidence-offset-second-line` shapes KILLED firsthand by the new row. P3-u/z pinned as bounds (`TestNormalizeNullOptionalBoolsDecodeAsFalse`, `TestNormalizeUnknownTypeNullBodyProjectsOpaque`); P3-v rows shipped (`body_text_number`, `body_live_attestation_string`, `body_missing_text` + 3 narrowings, the required gate pinned by its message); P3-w low edge pinned (`empty_directive` + `N-directive-empty`); P3-x `doc.go` nine→ten; P3-y declined-cosmetic with rationale (uniform member+line error shape is AC-pinned; the clonebundle helper wording at `session.go:527` is accepted sibling production, behavior verified correct); P3-aa MANIFEST self-entry dropped. No production change: test-plus-matrix only.\\n- REV4 REFRESH: trunk moved `c3aae73`→`42d5a95` (sibling STORY-260830-ptxkqe landed) before this run, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `42d5a95`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay for both checkpoints); the audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/axpane`, `internal/termbind`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/fencing`, `internal/terminalbackend`) and MERGED the five co-owned files (LOGBOOK newest-first, README figures+prose, ownership registry 152 cases/74 rows with every trunk row intact, the four pin tests); `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` re-derived via the gate as `614eb55d…` (command+output in results); `tracecheck` green `70/574` with `--section 7.8`/`10.2` admitted. AC: 47 of 47 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests (matrix rev4).\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2056mm rev3 — Binding-parser rework: closed-shape arms, identity pre-transform walk, stated bounds\\n- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev2 (no P1; P2-1 production at the Binding parser, five P3; the reviewer reproduced the v4 payloads, evidence/identity/recovery/authority behavior, the registry re-pin, and the harness 30/30 twice — all kept). P2-1: `ParseTerminalBinding` now enforces `protocol_version` major 1 (`isProtocolMajorOne` over the landed semver grammar, verdict-agreed with `CheckVersionTuple` on a 14-version corpus) and `extensions == {}` (landed strict frame, zero members) per the §4.B table, and `bindingIdentity` refuses JSON numbers at any depth plus nested duplicate members before the JCS transform (strict UseNumber decode with per-depth dup refusal, mirroring the landed terminalbackend decode+walk — digest-equality and verdict agreement pinned, including a numeric extension value). Every member arm of the table is now driven negatively through the entry (37-subtest battery with code+detail pins) with six new narrowing rows (major, extensions, number, nested-dup, supersedes, pre-read generation bound). P3-2: `EmitResumed` checkpoint/pair binding stated explicitly as a caller bound with a boundary-pinning test (fabricated checkpoint appends; fold reports it newest). P3-3: generation-bound-before-read witness committed with its row. P3-4: pre-scan harness notes corrected to the documented redundancy, README bootstrap sentence corrected to the plain refusal, `resolve.go` \\\"every failure\\\" scoped to resolution failures, row 57 / 5.2#18 restated as a bound, descriptor test added to the identity-exact case. P3-5: restore/terminate-stale execution deferred to a Story follow-up task (no board task exists yet — no brief assigned it); the kkh1an `HandoffFailed` note is NOT APPLICABLE (this leaf wires no reporter).\\n- CORRECTION to the rev1 entry's F2 (appended, history preserved): \\\"the mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain refusals)\\\" is wrong for the two body surfaces — the landed `ParseMutationContext`/`ParseStatusBody` refuse a forbidden identity with the SAME pinned `terminal_backend_protocol_error`; the pre-scans add only the Go error type (`*terminalbackend.Error`), and no wrapper exists for the bootstrap surface at all (landed `Store.Bind` refuses plain and uncoded). The wrappers stay as a documented redundancy with corrected notes.\\n- F1: a major-1 selection over an already-validated semver needs no integer parse — the major is the digit run before the first dot, so prefix `1.` is exact with no saturation class for huge foreign majors; the 14-version agreement battery against `CheckVersionTuple` (grammar faults, majors 0/2/3/10, a 2^64-scale major, prerelease/build spellings) proves no second model.\\n- F2: `bindingIdentity`'s old \\\"no number can reach the digest by check ordering\\\" comment was false exactly where extension values are untyped — the pre-transform walk must be structural (decode + walk), not an ordering claim; the direct-identity hostile battery (numbers, nested dups, trailing data, depth/size caps) pins the walk independently of the member arms that now fire first.\\n- AC: 65 of 66 rows driven through production entries by named tests (row 57 restated as a bound — no v1-v3-only reader exists on trunk; rows 61–66 are the rework rows; matrix in `internal/termbind/TRACEABILITY.md`). MUTATION EVIDENCE: 34 narrowing mutants plus one supplementary arm-delete row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 36/36 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical. Registry: 5.2 gap reworded to the row-57 bound, eight test citations added across four cases with mirror updates, digest re-derived `b09b5b9f…` (canonical bytes 167094), tracecheck green `63/574` with identical section ratios. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2056mm rev2 — Race-gate rework: per-subtest evidence universes\\n- REWORKED after the rev1 CR validation stopped at command 5/30 (`go test ./... -race`): one DATA RACE in `TestResolveEvidenceRequiresManifestAndProbe` — four parallel subtests shared a single `mapUniverse` while the two \\\"second\\\" cases extended it, racing the sibling `Lookup` reads (`resolve_test.go:172/181` vs `fixtures_test.go:490`). The race detector then failed the whole `termbind` package; every other package was green. Fix is test-only: each subtest builds its own `universeMap(t, world)` copy (rev2 delta vs the rev1 candidate is exactly this hunk, proven by whole-tree diff of the reconstructed rev1 tree). No production byte changed; the `N-resolve-manifest-count` killer still kills its narrowing mutant.\\n- VERIFIED: `go test ./internal/termbind/ -race -count=10` green (plus two more `-count=3` passes), siblings `axpane`/`terminstance` `-race` green, `mutant_harness.py` 30/30 on two identical passes, gofmt/vet/build clean, `task-board.config.json` byte-identical, trunk still `c3aae73` (no refresh). Full 30-command suite reruns automatically at handoff.\\n- F1: a shared mutable map across `t.Parallel()` subtests fails the entire package under `-race`, not just the racing test — every concurrently running test reports \\\"race detected during execution of test\\\", so one fixture race reads as fifteen failures. Fixture isolation per subtest is the fix; read-only sharing (as in `TestResolveEvidenceShapeBounds`) stays safe.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2056mm — Terminal binding events and recovery (story-final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/termbind` — the §4.1/4.B-4.D/5.2-Terminal-Events/7.A final leaf over the landed owners and the story's own `axpane`/`terminstance`: `ParseTerminalBinding` owns the Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object no parser existed for (ID recomputed before use, construction byte-agreed with the landed manifest admission); `CheckInstanceIdentity` + the operation-body pre-scans refuse the eight forbidden identity forms with the pinned protocol class on the Binding, descriptor (adopted landed entry), operation bodies, bootstrap binding, and attach receipts, with the CLI Result 4 surface a tripwire-pinned bound; `ResolveEvidence` resolves each v4 event's evidence IDs to exactly one Manifest, one Probe, and the Capability Evidence objects bound to the event tuple through the landed `Registry.AdmitProbe` (eleven foreign resolution targets refuse, substitution fails closed); `EmitTerminalCreated`/`EmitResumed` author the v4 payloads under a locally held lease with the digest as the opaque reference; `RecoverCreate` is read-only (absence / ONE child / unavailable+status_first, window from the fold newest); the attach receipt store records one durable receipt per client pair and emits neither event. Takeover selects an admitted backend with a new digest and event, append-only, never a fork; v1 readers stay inert.\\n- F1: the producer's \\\"§13.1\\\" recovery rule lives at §4.1 lines 1395/1399 in the pinned v0.7.0 document (\\\"status plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one child\\\") — §13.1's eight measured clauses are launch-plan/boot-direct/argv rules owned by another story, so the registry binds `section:4.1` (new, sliver 1/5) and leaves `section:13.1` untouched, with the mapping stated in the results.\\n- F2: a pre-scan gate is masked wherever the landed parser refuses with the identical code — the descriptor surface needed no wrapper (landed `AdmitProviderDescriptor` already pins `terminal_backend_protocol_error`), while the mutation-context/status/bootstrap surfaces needed one (landed plain refusals), and same-code reroutes (transport enum, evidence protocol arm, foreign-kind classification) need detail assertions or the mutant survives behind the landed twin.\\n- F3: the registry needed a reviewed-new-bindings extension — `assertNewBindingsAreReviewed` admitted only unevidenced stubs for sections the trunk baseline never bound, so `section:4.1` carries proof through a new `storyNewV070Bindings` list with literal matching plus clause remeasurement, mirroring the existing upgrade lists; seven new acceptance cases, four upgraded bindings (4.B/4.D/5.2 slivers, 7.A partial), digest re-pinned, tracecheck `63/574`.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 19747,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4937,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
