tory-final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/termbind` — the §4.1/4.B-4.D/5.2-Terminal-Events/7.A final leaf over the landed owners and the story's own `axpane`/`terminstance`: `ParseTerminalBinding` owns the Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 closed object no parser existed for (ID recomputed before use, construction byte-agreed with the landed manifest admission); `CheckInstanceIdentity` + the operation-body pre-scans refuse the eight forbidden identity forms with the pinned protocol class on the Binding, descriptor (adopted landed entry), operation bodies, bootstrap binding, and attach receipts, with the CLI Result 4 surface a tripwire-pinned bound; `ResolveEvidence` resolves each v4 event's evidence IDs to exactly one Manifest, one Probe, and the Capability Evidence objects bound to the event tuple through the landed `Registry.AdmitProbe` (eleven foreign resolution targets refuse, substitution fails closed); `EmitTerminalCreated`/`EmitResumed` author the v4 payloads under a locally held lease with the digest as the opaque reference; `RecoverCreate` is read-only (absence / ONE child / unavailable+status_first, window from the fold newest); the attach receipt store records one durable receipt per client pair and emits neither event. Takeover selects an admitted backend with a new digest and event, append-only, never a fork; v1 readers stay inert.\\n- F1: the producer's \\\"§13.1\\\" recovery rule lives at §4.1 lines 1395/1399 in the pinned v0.7.0 document (\\\"status plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one child\\\") — §13.1's eight measured clauses are launch-plan/boot-direct/argv rules owned by another story, so the registry binds `section:4.1` (new, sliver 1/5) and leaves `section:13.1` untouched, with the mapping stated in the results.\\n- F2: a pre-scan gate is masked wherever the landed parser refuses with the identical code — the descriptor surface needed no wrapper (landed `AdmitProviderDescriptor` already pins `terminal_backend_protocol_error`)